# Network-monitoring messages arriving on a call, hand-built from RFC 5456
# §6.7 / §9.1, §9.2 (notes §12, "Network monitoring flows"):
#
#       <== PING     "Receipt of a PING requires an acknowledging PONG" (§6.7.2)
#   PONG ==>         echoing the PING's time-stamp (§6.7.3)
#       <== LAGRQ
#   LAGRP ==>        "MUST send the same time-stamp it received" (§6.7.5)
#
# Our source call number is 1, the peer's 0x0042. Neither message changes call
# state, so this fixture is valid at any point after the NEW.

# PING, ts 1000 (0x3e8), OSeq 0, ISeq 1, type 0x06 IAX, subclass 0x02 (§8.4).
8042 0001 000003e8 00 01 06 02

# LAGRQ, ts 2000 (0x7d0), OSeq 1, ISeq 2, type 0x06 IAX, subclass 0x0b (§8.4).
# ISeq is 2 because our PONG carried OSeqno 1.
8042 0001 000007d0 01 02 06 0b
